Git Interview Questions and Answers
1. What is Git?
Git is a distributed version control system used to track changes in source code, collaborate with developers, and maintain project history.
2. Why do we use Git?
To track changes, collaborate with teams, restore previous versions, manage features using branches, and maintain project history.
3. What is Version Control?
A system that records changes to files over time.
4. Difference between Git and GitHub?
Git is a version control system; GitHub is a cloud platform for hosting Git repositories.
5. What is a Repository?
A project folder tracked by Git.
6. What is the .git folder?
Stores commits, branches, configuration and Git history.
7. How do you configure Git?
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
8. Check configuration?
git config --list
9. Check Git version?
git --version
10. What does git init do?
Initializes a Git repository.
11. What does git status show?
Repository status, current branch, staged, unstaged and untracked files.
12. What is an untracked file?
A file not yet tracked by Git.
13. What is the staging area?
Temporary area before committing.
14. git add . vs git add <file>?
First stages all changes; second stages only one file.
15. What is a commit?
A snapshot of your project.
16. Commit command?
git commit -m "message"
17. Why meaningful commit messages?
They explain what changed and why.
18. View history?
git log or git log --oneline
19. What is a remote repository?
A repository hosted on GitHub or another server.
20. Connect local repo?
git remote add origin <url>
21. Verify remote?
git remote -v
22. Upload code?
git push origin main
23. git push vs git push -u?
-u sets upstream branch.
24. What is a branch?
Independent line of development.
25. Why branches?
To isolate features and fixes.
26. List branches?
git branch
27. Create branch?
git branch feature-name
28. Switch branch?
git switch feature-name
29. Create and switch?
git switch -c feature-name
30. Multiple branches?
Yes, one repository can have many branches.
31. Do branch changes appear automatically?
No, only after merging.
32. What is merging?
Combining changes from one branch into another.
33. Merge command?
git merge feature-name
34. What is a merge conflict?
Occurs when Git cannot automatically merge changes.
35. Resolve conflicts?
Edit, remove markers, test, stage and commit.
36. What is git pull?
Fetches and merges changes.
37. What is git fetch?
Downloads changes without merging.
38. Pull vs Fetch?
Pull = fetch + merge; Fetch = download only.
39. Daily workflow?
Pull, branch, code, add, commit, push, PR, merge.
40. Common commands?
git status, git add ., git commit, git push, git pull, git branch, git switch, git merge, git log
41. Wrong branch?
Move changes to a new branch or stash them.
42. Forgot to commit?
Commit or stash before switching if required.
43. Pushed wrong code?
Fix with a new commit or use git revert.
44. Why not work on main?
To keep the stable branch safe.
45. Calculator workflow?
Initialize, commit, push, create feature branches, push, PR, merge.
